evenue), so pricing power is hard to come by."],"mkt":["The shares have drifted lower, down 11% over the past year excluding the latest month.","The price sits mid-way through its 52-week range, 17% below the high.","With annualised volatility of 28% and a beta of 0.91, it moves roughly with the market.","About $55.4M trades a day, enough to build a position.","In past sell-offs it fell 41% in the 2020 crash, 40% in the 2022 bear market and 75% in 2008."],"val":["The price sits above its DCF fair value of $125 (margin of safety -37%), so there is no valuation cushion.","The fair-value models disagree (dispersion 17%), and the Monte Carlo range runs $89.46 to $178 (P10-P90), so treat the estimate as noisy.","On multiples it looks expensive against Industrials peers: P/FCF 29.1 vs 22.3 (sector median).","Against its own history it is dear: the EBIT multiple sits 43% above its 10-year median.","Earnings yields are thin: an FCF yield of 3.4% (below the risk-free rate) and an EBIT/EV of 5.7% (vs the 8% bar).","The 11 covering analysts target $200 on average, 17% above the price, well away from the model's fair value."],"prof":["ROIC of 22% clears the cost of capital of 9.1% by 13pp, the mark of a value creator; returns have swung a lot from year to year (CV 0.45).","It runs a 36% gross margin and converts 15% of revenue into free cash flow.","Earnings quality looks solid: a Piotroski score of 9/9 and cash conversion of 1.15x.","ROE of 34% comes mostly from margins and asset turnover rather than leverage (2.1x equity multiplier).","It spends 1.0% of revenue on R&D and 1.4% on stock compensation."],"hlth":["Leverage is conservative at 0.5x net debt to EBITDA ($112.7M of cash against $406.7M of debt), with interest covered 13.1x.","No distress or manipulation flags (Altman Z 7.2, in the safe zone)."],"growth":["Revenue has compounded at 9.5% over 3 years, 11.6% over 5 years and -3.9% over 10 years, so growth is decelerating, and it has been lumpy (year-to-year swings of 17%).","At current returns, reinvesting 4% of profits supports about 0.9% a year of fundamental growth, too little to drive meaningful growth.","Free cash flow has compounded 8.5% a year over five years.","Margins are expanding (+1.3% trend).","Capex roughly matches depreciation (0.9x, 6.7% of sales), a maintenance pace.","Its Rule of 40 score is 25, below the 40 that marks a healthy growth business."],"own":["Insiders own a modest 1.6%, and reported institutional holdings exceed 100% of shares (a sign of heavy share lending).","It returns 2.6% a year to shareholders (1.8% in buybacks and 0.9% in dividends).","The share count has shrunk 2.4% a year over five years, steadily raising each holder's stake."],"people":["With about 4,100 employees, each generates about $395K of revenue, in line with the Industrials median, and productivity has fallen 4.0% a year.","That works out to $60K of free cash flow per employee.","CEO pay is $1.2M (3x revenue per employee), and compensation governance scores well (1/10, lower is better).","Stock compensation averages $5K per employee."]},"profile":{"v":"AVOID","conv":76,"head":"Avoid: priced 37% above its fair value of $125.","pros":["Model rating LEAN BUY (composite 44, gates 12/24)","ROIC 22.2% vs WACC 9.1%","FCF margin 15.2%","Revenue grew 11.6%/yr over 5y","Net debt/EBITDA 0.5x"],"cons":["Trades 37% above fair value of $125","P/FCF 29.1x vs sector 22.3x"],"flags":["Priced 37% above its fair value of $125"],"need":[],"buy_below":106.34,"vc":{"base":125.1,"base_src":"dcf","bear":89.46,"bull":178.41,"alt_median":109.15,"n_alt":3,"gap":0.1461,"dispersion":0.1701,"level":"MEDIUM","why":[]},"med":{"pe":23.2692,"ev_ebitda":13.319,"pfcf":22.2778,"pb":3.0551,"roic":0.1001,"gross_margin":0.2851,"fcf_margin":0.068,"div_yield":0.0147}},"ticker":"AWI","date":"2026-11-06"}